<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Description>
      The EF-free half of persistence's schema-family surface, shared by every host with every package it loads
      (#2143; ADR 0067, amended 2026-09-29): the reflection-only reader of schema-family declarations, the finalization
      record's model and status, what a host observed of it, the finalization gate's view of the fleet, and the
      registry a container's gates are found in, and IEfModuleRefusal, what a module's refusal to activate says of itself.
      It references no EF Core, no database engine and no Elsa project, so a
      host that carries no EF (ADR 0076) can compose cluster membership over it, and an EF module whose own copy of
      Elsa.Persistence.EntityFramework Nuplane loads privately still exchanges these types with the host.
    </Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- IChangeToken, the fleet's change signal. -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Primitives" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
